 Might make most sense to be sub one,

51
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,160
 but it's not, it's sub zero.

52
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,960
 But just remember that.

53
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:22,640
 And so we have this operator called the index operator.

54
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,960
 And it's square brackets.

55
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:28,760
 So you know, fruit is a variable

56
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:30,640
 that contains the string banana.

57
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:33,680
 And then fruit sub one is the character

58
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,960
 that's in position one.

59
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,240
 Now that actually is the second character.

60
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,320
 I'll keep reminding you until I get tired of reminding you.

61
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:43,200
 And so that assigns A, the letter A,

62
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:48,200
 into, I mean, the letter A into the variable letter.

63
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,200
 Of course that's a badly chosen,

64
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,860
 it's either a well chosen variable name

65
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:53,460
 or a badly chosen variable name.

66
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:56,120
 And the thing that goes inside this

67
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,280
 can either be a constant or it can be an expression.

68
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,120
 So this is X equals three.

69
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:03,160
 And then fruit sub X minus one, well that means two,

70
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:05,120
 which is position two, which is an N.

71
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,600
 And so that gives us an N.

72
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,640
 So the index is an operator.

73
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,740
 And you can add this bracket syntax

74
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:13,880
 to the end of a string variable.

75
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:18,400
 You can't index beyond the length of the string.

76
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,800
 So if I say Zot sub five, well,

77
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,800
 there's only three characters, which means zero, one, two,

78
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,880
 but sub five doesn't work.

79
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,480
 And of course we get a happy little trace back.

80
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:32,540
 So you have to be careful when you're starting

81
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:33,680
 to pull stuff out of strings.

82
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,320
 Although some of the things allow it,

83
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:38,400
 some of them don't, and then you'll kinda get used to that.

84
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,240
 We can ask how long a string is.

85
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:43,120
 And so we use the len function,

86
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,200
 and we pass the string variable,

87
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,400
 and we pass it into len as parameter,

88
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,880
 and len gives us back the length of the string,

89
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,480
 not the position.

90
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:55,280
 So it's zero through len minus one.

91
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,440
 So it's zero through length minus one.

92
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,900
 So length is just another function

93
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,240
 that we've been doing functions now for a while.

94
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:06,560
 You pass in a parameter, and then len does some work,

95
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,720
 and out comes six, and that goes back into X,

96
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,720
 'cause the function has a residual value.

97
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:14,840
 It just happens to be a built-in function.

98
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:19,080
 And so somewhere deep inside Python

99
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,920
 there is code that takes this,

100
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:24,360
 and somebody wrote a loop or looked something up,

101
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:28,160
 and then returned a return value and sent back a six

102
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,480
 to go into our X variable.

103
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:34,080
 And so a function is there, and like I said,

104
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,440
 we've been using this for a while.

105
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,680
 Another thing we tend to do is to look through strings

106
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,880
 and look at strings and dig data out of strings.

107
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:45,320
 Python is excellent for doing sort of these kinds

